Q: using Vertex AI Embedding in Spring Boot App A: <p>The following error</p>
<pre><code>Caused by: java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: org.springframework.core.retry.RetryListener
</code></pre>
<p>hints at a missing class.</p>
<p><code>RetryTemplate</code> needs to be available in the class path.</p>
<p>The <code>org.springframework.core.retry.RetryListener</code> class is one imported from <code>spring-core</code> and not <a href="https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-retry/blob/main/src/main/java/org/springframework/retry/RetryListener.java" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>org.springframework.retry.RetryListener</code></a></p>
<p>You can add <code>spring-core</code> as a dependency to your <code>pom.xml</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-core&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;7.0.3&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Alternatively, I strongly suggest using the <a href="https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/blob/v4.0.2/starter/spring-boot-starter/build.gradle" rel="nofollow noreferrer">4.0.2 spring boot starter</a>. It includes in <code>spring-core</code>, pre-configuration for logging and enables auto-configuration.</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-starter&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;4.0.2&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
